[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] ## Step 1: Understand the Problem
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] The problem asks for the maximum possible order of an element in the symmetric group S_n, where n = 10.
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] 
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] ## Step 2: Recall the Formula for the Order of an Element in S_n
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] The order of an element a in S_n is given by the formula: |S_n| = n! / (n - r)!, where r is the number of fixed points of a.
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] 
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] ## Step 3: Determine the Number of Fixed Points for an Element in S_10
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] To find the maximum possible order, we need to find the number of fixed points of an element in S_10. This can be done by counting the number of permutations of the elements in S_10 that leave the same element unchanged.
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] 
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] ## Step 4: Count the Number of Permutations of S_10
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] The number of permutations of S_10 is given by 10! = 3628800.
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] 
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] ## Step 5: Calculate the Maximum Possible Order
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] The maximum possible order is given by the formula: |S_n| = n! / (n - r)! = 10! / (10 - r)! = 3628800 / (10 - 1)! = 3628800 / 9! = 3628800 / 362880 = 10.
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] 
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] ## Step 6: Select the Correct Answer
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] Since the maximum possible order is 10, the correct answer is C. 30.
