[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] ## Step 1: Understand the Problem
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] The problem asks to find the sum of two given polynomials in the polynomial ring Z_8[x], which means the coefficients are taken modulo 8.
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] 
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] ## Step 2: Identify the Polynomials
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] The given polynomials are f(x) = 4x - 5 and g(x) = 2x^2 - 4x + 2.
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] 
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] ## Step 3: Convert Polynomials to Z_8[x]
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] To find the sum of the polynomials, we need to convert them to Z_8[x]. This means we replace x with x modulo 8.
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] 
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] ## Step 4: Convert f(x) to Z_8[x]
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] f(x) = 4x - 5 becomes f(x) = 4x - 5 ≡ 4x - 5 (mod 8).
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] 
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] ## Step 5: Convert g(x) to Z_8[x]
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] g(x) = 2x^2 - 4x + 2 becomes g(x) = 2x^2 - 4x + 2 ≡ 2x^2 - 4x + 2 (mod 8).
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] 
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] ## Step 6: Find the Sum of the Polynomials
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] To find the sum, we add the two polynomials: (4x - 5) + (2x^2 - 4x + 2) ≡ 2x^2 + 2x - 3 (mod 8).
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] 
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] ## Step 7: Simplify the Sum
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] The sum is already simplified modulo 8.
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] 
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] ## Step 8: Match the Result to the Options
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] The simplified sum 2x^2 + 2x - 3 corresponds to option B.
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] 
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] The final answer is: $\boxed{B}$
