[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] ## Step 8: Conclusion
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] Since p = 2 does not divide c and gcd(c, d) is not 1, the polynomial does not satisfy the conditions of Eisenstein's Criterion.
