[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] ## Step 2: Recall the definition of a group
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] A group is a set G with a binary operation (often denoted as multiplication or addition) that satisfies four properties: closure, associativity, identity element, and inverse element.
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] 
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] ## Step 3: Analyze the given condition
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] The given condition implies that for any two elements a and b in G, the inverse of their product ab is equal to the inverse of a times the inverse of b. This is a characteristic property of groups.
