[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] ## Step 2: Recall the Condition for a Field
[INFO] 10-06 17:22:56 run_experiments_1.py:103] A field is a commutative ring with unity and in which every non-zero element has a multiplicative inverse. In the context of polynomial rings, this means that for Z_3[x]/(x^3 + x^2 + c) to be a field, the polynomial x^3 + x^2 + c must be irreducible over Z_3.
